# star24full k=9 — 2026-08-07

First run to use DEPTH-2 sharding (EU_SHARD_D2=8, N=360, 9 slots). Safe for a NEW k: depth-2 changes
only which representative of an isomorphism class gets printed, and k=9 records do not exist yet, so
no shipped vertype key moves. The k<=8 prefix of this run will NOT byte-match the stored digests for
the same reason; it is verified instead with the order-insensitive block-multiset comparison
(scratchpad/verify-d2.py), the gate that passed at k=5, 6 and 7.

Projection from the ladder (k=8 was 4140 CPU-s at a 3.73 time ratio): ~15,000 CPU-s. At the measured
depth-2 floor of ~6% that is roughly 30-35 min wall on 9 slots, against ~50 min for depth-1.
Count projection ~1.9x k=8 => ~11,800, cumulative ~24,200.

